---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const title = "Counter-Conditioning San Jacinto | Good Doggos";
const description = "Rewire your dog's emotional brain with counter-conditioning and desensitization in San Jacinto. Change how your dog feels about triggers through leadership.";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Service",
  "name": "Counter-Conditioning & Desensitization",
  "description": description,
  "provider": {
    "@type": "LocalBusiness",
    "name": "Good Doggos",
    "url": "https://gooddoggos.com",
    "telephone": "+19514016252",
    "address": {
      "@type": "PostalAddress",
      "addressLocality": "San Jacinto",
      "addressRegion": "CA",
      "addressCountry": "US"
    }
  },
  "areaServed": {
    "@type": "AdministrativeArea",
    "name": "Riverside County"
  },
  "url": "https://gooddoggos.com/services/counter-conditioning"
};
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)} />
  </Fragment>

  <!-- Hero Band -->
  <section class="bg-primary-navy pt-32 pb-16 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <!-- Breadcrumb -->
      <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-body text-white/50 mt-6 mb-4" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/" class="text-accent-gold hover:text-accent-gold/80 underline font-semibold">Home</a>
        <span>&rsaquo;</span>
        <a href="/services/behavioral-modification" class="text-accent-gold hover:text-accent-gold/80 underline font-semibold">Behavioral Modification</a>
        <span>&rsaquo;</span>
        <span class="text-white/80 truncate">Counter-Conditioning</span>
      </nav>

      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-heading font-bold text-white leading-tight mb-6">
        Counter-Conditioning and Desensitization in San Jacinto
      </h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Body Content -->
  <section class="py-16 px-4 bg-[#FCF9FA]">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-12">
      
      <!-- Main Content -->
      <div class="prose max-w-none">
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          If your dog loses their mind every time a neighbor starts a lawnmower or an Amazon driver pulls into your San Jacinto driveway, you’re dealing with a deep-seated emotional response.
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          These sudden outbursts are symptoms of a dog that is genuinely convinced the world is ending. Because we are professionals, we do not guess or hand out generic advice. We must evaluate your dog in person to understand their specific triggers before we can begin rewiring their emotional brain through a balanced approach.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-heading font-bold text-primary-navy mt-12 mb-6">
          Rewiring the Emotional Brain
        </h2>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          At Good Doggos, I don't just mask symptoms; I change how your dog feels about their triggers. Desensitization is about exposure at a level your dog can handle—starting at a distance where they see the "scary thing" but don't blow up. Counter-conditioning is where we pair that trigger with something high-value. 
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          But I differ from the "strictly positive" crowd: I use a balanced approach. While I use plenty of praise, I also maintain clear boundaries. If a dog tries to escalate into a dangerous lunging fit, I use calibrated leash corrections to provide the structure they need to stay under threshold and actually learn.
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          I remember a dog that was terrified of delivery trucks in a local San Jacinto neighborhood. By using my helper dog Simba as a neutral role model, we showed the dog that he could look at the truck and then look at us for a reward. Simba's calm indifference gave the other dog permission to relax. It wasn't about the treat; it was about the leadership Simba and I provided.
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          I’ve spent 8 years perfecting this balance. I don't stay in a sterile room; I get out into the San Jacinto heat and work where the real triggers are. Whether it's cyclists near Valley-Wide Regional Park or the heavy traffic on State Street, I show your dog that they can remain neutral and calm. I want a dog that sees a trigger, looks at you, and decides it’s no big deal.
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6 font-bold">
          Ready to stop avoiding the world and start enjoying it with your dog? I'm here to help.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════
     CTA BAND
══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="relative overflow-hidden bg-[#FBF1E9]" style="border-top: 1px solid #E6DAC6;">
  <div class="w-full h-[3px]" style="background: linear-gradient(to right, #0F6D72, #D1B27F, #0F6D72);"></div>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-20 md:py-24 text-center">
    <p class="text-[11px] font-bold tracking-[0.25em] uppercase mb-4" style="color: rgba(15,109,114,0.60);">Your Dog Is Next</p>
    <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-heading font-bold mb-4" style="color: #0B2744;">
      Ready to See What's Possible?<br/>
      <span class="headline-accent" style="color: #D1B27F; font-style: italic; font-weight: 700;">Start With a Free Assessment.</span>
    </h2>
    <p class="text-base mb-10 max-w-lg mx-auto" style="color: rgba(17,32,50,0.60);">
      Tell us about your dog. We'll do an honest assessment and point you toward the right program — or tell you if we're not the right fit.
    </p>
    <a href="/apply"
       class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 font-bold text-sm tracking-widest uppercase rounded-full transition-all duration-200 hover:-translate-y-0.5"
       style="background: #D1B27F; color: #0B2744; padding: 18px 44px; box-shadow: 0 6px 24px rgba(209,178,127,0.35);">
      Apply for Free Behavioral Assessment →
    </a>
    <p class="mt-4 text-xs" style="color: rgba(17,32,50,0.40);">Takes less than 3 minutes · No commitment required</p>
  </div>
</div>
</Layout>
